<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<package xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/packaging/2011/08/nuspec.xsd">
  <metadata minClientVersion="2.12">
    <id>MimeKit</id>
    <version>5.0.0</version>
    <title>MimeKit</title>
    <authors>Jeffrey Stedfast</authors>
    <owners>Jeffrey Stedfast</owners>
    <license type="expression">MIT</license>
    <projectUrl>https://www.mimekit.net</projectUrl>
    <repository type="git" url="https://github.com/jstedfast/MimeKit" />
    <icon>icons\mimekit-50.png</icon>
    <requireLicenseAcceptance>false</requireLicenseAcceptance>
    <description>
      MimeKit is an Open Source library for creating and parsing MIME, S/MIME and PGP messages on desktop and mobile platforms. It also supports parsing of Unix mbox files.

      As of v5.0, MimeKit is a meta-package that references both MimeKit.Core (MIME creation and parsing) and MimeKit.Cryptography (OpenPGP, S/MIME, DKIM, ARC and DMARC support). This preserves backwards compatibility for consumers that expect cryptography support out of the box. If you do not need cryptography, reference MimeKit.Core directly instead.

      API documentation can be found on the web at http://www.mimekit.net/docs

      For those that need SMTP, POP3 or IMAP support, check out https://github.com/jstedfast/MailKit    </description>
    <summary>An Open Source library for creating and parsing MIME, S/MIME and PGP messages on desktop and mobile platforms.</summary>
    <releaseNotes>
MimeKit 5.0 is a major release containing a number of breaking changes. See https://github.com/jstedfast/MimeKit/blob/master/ReleaseNotes.md for the complete list of changes and migration notes.

* MimeKit is now a meta-package that references MimeKit.Core (MIME creation and parsing) and MimeKit.Cryptography (S/MIME, PGP/MIME, DKIM, ARC and DMARC). MimeKitLite has been retired; use MimeKit.Core instead.
* Promoted the new MIME parser (formerly ExperimentalMimeParser) to MimeParser. The previous implementation is available as LegacyMimeParser.
* CryptographyContext no longer registers a default S/MIME context. Applications must explicitly register the context they want. This makes MimeKit AOT-compatible.
* Added DMARC validation, MIME compliance violation reporting, a redesigned TNEF API with TnefWriter, and the RtfToText and RtfToHtml text converters.
* Numerous performance improvements and bug fixes.
    </releaseNotes>
    <copyright>.NET Foundation and Contributors</copyright>
    <language>en-US</language>
    <tags>mime encryption arc dkim dmarc security smime s/mime openpgp pgp mbox mail email parser tnef</tags>
    <readme>docs\README.md</readme>
